## 🔹 Arrays (1–8)

1. Find the second largest element in an array.
2. Remove duplicates from a sorted array (in-place).
3. Rotate an array to the right by *k* steps.
4. Find the maximum subarray sum (Kadane’s Algorithm).
5. Merge two sorted arrays without using extra space.
6. Find the missing number in an array of size *n* containing numbers from 1 to *n*.
7. Find all leaders in an array (elements greater than all elements to their right).
8. Rearrange array so that positive and negative numbers alternate.

---

## 🔹 Strings (9–16)

9. Check if a string is a palindrome.
10. Find the first non-repeating character in a string.
11. Check if two strings are anagrams.
12. Reverse words in a given sentence.
13. Implement `strStr()` (substring search).
14. Longest common prefix among an array of strings.
15. Find the longest palindromic substring.
16. Group anagrams together.

---

## 🔹 Linked List (17–23)

17. Reverse a singly linked list.
18. Detect a cycle in a linked list (Floyd’s cycle detection).
19. Merge two sorted linked lists.
20. Remove the Nth node from the end of a list.
21. Find the middle of a linked list.
22. Check if a linked list is a palindrome.
23. Flatten a multilevel linked list.

---

## 🔹 Stack & Queue (24–29)

24. Implement a stack using queues.
25. Implement a queue using stacks.
26. Check for balanced parentheses.
27. Next greater element in an array.
28. Implement LRU Cache.
29. Evaluate a postfix expression.

---

## 🔹 Recursion & Backtracking (30–35)

30. Generate all subsets of a set.
31. Generate all permutations of a string.
32. Solve the N-Queens problem.
33. Solve Sudoku.
34. Word search in a 2D board.
35. Combination Sum problem.

---

## 🔹 Trees (36–42)

36. Inorder, Preorder, and Postorder traversal (recursive & iterative).
37. Level order traversal of a binary tree.
38. Check if a binary tree is height-balanced.
39. Diameter of a binary tree.
40. Lowest common ancestor (LCA) in a binary tree.
41. Validate if a binary tree is a Binary Search Tree (BST).
42. Find kth smallest element in a BST.

---

## 🔹 Graphs (43–47)

43. Implement DFS and BFS.
44. Detect a cycle in an undirected graph.
45. Detect a cycle in a directed graph.
46. Find shortest path using Dijkstra’s algorithm.
47. Topological sort (Kahn’s Algorithm).

---

## 🔹 Dynamic Programming (48–50)

48. Climbing Stairs problem.
49. Longest Increasing Subsequence (LIS).
50. 0/1 Knapsack problem.

